The CIA maintains a digital copy of the full correction table for the specific degree distribution estimated from the colony’s communication logs. Prior to any rotation, the current population size N and clustering \mathcal{C} are used to look up p_c^{\text{eff}}(N,\mathcal{C}). The planned post‑rotation retention probability p must exceed this value by the safety margin \Delta_{\text{FS}} that guarantees, via Lemma F.1, a fragmentation probability below 10^{-4}. If p falls short, the rotation is vetoed.

